ref_completion:
We need to expand the expression $(2x^5 + 3x^2)(x^4 - 4x^2 + 3x - 8)$. We distribute each term in the first factor across the terms in the second factor:
\begin{align*} (2x^5 + 3x^2)(x^4 - 4x^2 + 3x - 8) &= 2x^5(x^4 - 4x^2 + 3x - 8) + 3x^2(x^4 - 4x^2 + 3x - 8) \\ &= 2x^9 - 8x^7 + 6x^6 - 16x^5 + 3x^6 - 12x^4 + 9x^3 - 24x^2 \\ &= 2x^9 - 8x^7 + (6x^6 + 3x^6) - 16x^5 - 12x^4 + 9x^3 - 24x^2 \\ &= 2x^9 - 8x^7 + 9x^6 - 16x^5 - 12x^4 + 9x^3 - 24x^2\end{aligned}
Thus, the expanded form is $2x^9 - 8x^7 + 9x^6 - 16x^5 - 12x^4 + 9x^3 - 24x^2$.

\boxed{2x^9 - 8x^7 + 9x^6 - 16x^5 - 12x^4 + 9x^3 - 24x^2}

